<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs exclude filter for NexusPiercer.

  Every entry below must state WHY it is suppressed. An unexplained suppression is
  indistinguishable from a bug someone hid, and this repository already demonstrates what
  happens when a gate's configuration is never read by a human.

  Do not add blanket <Match><Bug category="..."/></Match> entries. Suppress a specific
  pattern in a specific class, or fix the finding.
-->
<FindBugsFilter
        xmlns="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/spotbugs/spotbugs/4.8.3/spotbugs/etc/findbugsfilter.xsd">

    <!-- Generated Avro classes are not ours to fix. -->
    <Match>
        <Source name="~.*[\\/]generated-sources[\\/].*"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Source name="~.*[\\/]generated-test-sources[\\/].*"/>
    </Match>

    <!--
      NOT DEAD, AND NOT ABOUT GROOVY. Measured 2026-08-11 while removing the last of the Groovy
      toolchain. The previous comment here claimed these were "Groovy-compiled classes" carrying
      "compiler-synthesised members" and predicted the block would become dead once the Groovy
      sources were ported. Both claims are false:

        * All five classes are, and were already, ordinary Java in src/main. src/main went
          Groovy-free well before this change, so nothing about porting src/test/groovy could
          have retired this block.
        * Deleting the block moves SpotBugs 241 -> 251. It is actively suppressing 10 findings
          in hand-written Java, none of which is a compiler artefact:
              UPM_UNCALLED_PRIVATE_METHOD  (5) AvroReconstructor.calculateArraySize,
                                               AvroReconstructor.reconstructNestedArrayOfRecords,
                                               AvroReconstructor.unwrapUnion,
                                               GAvroSchemaFlattener.isNullable,
                                               MapFlattener.flattenSingleValue
              SIC_INNER_SHOULD_BE_STATIC_ANON (3) AvroReconstructor$1, AvroReconstructor$2,
                                               GAvroSchemaFlattener$1
              RCN_REDUNDANT_NULLCHECK_OF_NONNULL_VALUE (2) AvroReconstructor
                                               .reconstructNestedRecordFromArray

      The five UPM findings are dead private methods in the shipped library and deserve a
      deliberate follow-up: either they are genuinely unreachable and should be deleted, or a
      caller was lost and something is silently not running. They are NOT fixed here, because
      changing library behaviour inside a build-tooling removal would hide the change.

      The block is retained only to hold the 241 ceiling; the ceiling may not be raised. It has
      been NARROWED from five suppressed patterns to the three that actually fire —
      NP_LOAD_OF_KNOWN_NULL_VALUE and UUF_UNUSED_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD suppressed nothing and
      were a standing exemption for future code. Count after narrowing is unchanged at 241.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Class name="io.github.pierce.AvroReconstructor"/>
            <Class name="io.github.pierce.GAvroSchemaFlattener"/>
            <Class name="io.github.pierce.JsonFlattener"/>
            <Class name="io.github.pierce.JsonReconstructor"/>
            <Class name="io.github.pierce.MapFlattener"/>
        </Or>
        <Or>
            <Bug pattern="RCN_REDUNDANT_NULLCHECK_OF_NONNULL_VALUE"/>
            <Bug pattern="SIC_INNER_SHOULD_BE_STATIC_ANON"/>
            <Bug pattern="UPM_UNCALLED_PRIVATE_METHOD"/>
        </Or>
    </Match>

    <!--
      EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 fire on every builder and config object that stores or
      returns a caller-supplied collection. Defensive-copying all of them would add an
      allocation to the per-record path that the benchmark corpus is specifically designed to
      measure. Suppressed only for the immutable-by-contract config carriers; NOT suppressed
      globally.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Class name="~io\.github\.pierce\.converter\.ConversionConfig.*"/>
            <Class name="~io\.github\.pierce\..*\$.*Builder"/>
        </Or>
        <Or>
            <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/>
            <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
        </Or>
    </Match>

    <!--
      Two accessors on FlattenedField, named individually rather than by package so a future field
      that starts leaking state is not covered by inheritance from this entry.

      properties() returns the internal map ON PURPOSE. A LeafInterceptor annotates a leaf during
      the flatten — that is the whole point of the hook, documented on both types. A defensive copy
      would make every interceptor silently ineffective: the caller mutates a copy, sees no error,
      and gets an unenriched field. That is precisely the failure mode this repository keeps
      finding, so it is the copy that would be the bug here.

      schema() returns the Avro Schema. Schema is mutable via addProp, but it is also interned and
      shared throughout Avro itself; deep-copying one per leaf would cost a parse per field and
      still hand back something the caller could mutate. Callers must not mutate it — stated on
      the accessor.

      The other five findings SpotBugs raised against this package (SE_BAD_FIELD x2,
      UC_USELESS_OBJECT, SE_NO_SERIALVERSIONID) were fixed, not suppressed.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Class name="io.github.pierce.schema.FlattenedField"/>
        <Or>
            <Method name="properties"/>
            <Method name="schema"/>
        </Or>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/>
    </Match>

</FindBugsFilter>
